keywords:
  - just-in-time defect prediction
  - software defect prediction
  - machine learning
  - replication package
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a study of how realistic evaluation (chronological
  splits, label-latency handling, class-imbalance treatment, and effort-aware
  metrics) changes the measured performance of logistic regression, random
  forest, and XGBoost for just-in-time defect prediction on 19 projects from
  ApacheJIT and Kamei et al. It contains the leakage-checked pipeline, unit
  tests, result tables, figures, a data-download script, and a command-line
  prototype.
